WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.900
In the wave of Disney's live-action remakes,
one just might end up taking the cake when

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.780
it comes to critical success and audience
enjoyment.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:13.460
Yup, we're talking about Mulan a live-action
reimagining of the 1999 smash hit.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.800
This is everything you need to know about
the upcoming take on the beloved Disney classic.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.480
Audiences will have to wait until March 27,
2020 for Mulan's triumphant return to theaters

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.200
just over two decades after the original film's
release date in June of 1998.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.680
The 2020 release date isn't surprising, as
Disney already packed 2019 with remakes and

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.680
revivals of animated properties Dumbo, Aladdin,
The Lion King, Maleficent: Mistress of Evil,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.640
and Lady and the Tramp.

00:00:41.830 --> 00:00:45.640
With so many live-action films coming out
at once, it's nice that we'll get a little

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.220
bit of a breather before Mulan takes the stage.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:52.660
After all, it would be a shame for the film
to lose some luster simply because audiences

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.080
are suffering from live-action remake fatigue.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:01:00.140
One thing that's a bit surprising is the fact
that, while never on the docket for a 2019

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:04.420
release date, Mulan was actually originally
slated to hit the big screen before any of

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:05.940
the aforementioned titles.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.480
Once upon a time, the remake was supposed
to be released on November 2, 2018.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:13.140
Why shift the date by nearly a year and a
half?

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.880
Because it took over a year to find the right
actress to play the lead role.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.420
Once that was done, the film was locked into
the March 27th slot, and it looks like it'll

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.929
be making the rescheduled date without any
issues.

00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:29.630
So, how did the casting process end up pushing
the Mulan remake back by over a year?

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.889
It turns out that finding the perfect person
to play the lead role wasn't just challenging

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:36.500
it was about as difficult a task as possible.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.840
According to The Hollywood Reporter, Disney
enlisted a team of casting directors that

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.670
visited five continents, where they saw nearly
1,000 different candidates audition for the

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:46.160
role.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.660
Talk about doing your homework.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.280
It makes sense, though, as you don't meet
a girl like this every dynasty.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.840
The casting team wasn't just looking for actresses
who had passable martial arts skills and could

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.080
speak English fluently.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.060
They also made a top priority out of finding
someone who was ethnically Chinese, as well.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.740
After spending such a gargantuan amount of
time and effort, the team finally chose the

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:09.540
popular Chinese American actress Liu Yifei.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.810
The choice was a near-perfect one Liu Yifei
is talented and has already proven her acting

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:15.300
chops.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:19.460
Along with a string of other projects, the
actress has starred in The Forbidden Kingdom

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:24.280
and Outcast, both of which saw her holding
her own alongside well-established actors

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.960
like Jackie Chan, Nicolas Cage, and Jet Li.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.140
"I will bring honor to us all."

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:35.980
Having worked alongside him on 2008's The
Forbidden Kingdom, Liu Yifei is reteaming

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:37.600
with Jet Li for Mulan.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.880
The martial arts master has been tapped to
play the venerable Emperor of China.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:46.430
This is exciting news, even if it's a fairly
reserved role all things considered here's

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.690
hoping they can sneak him into a fight sequence
alongside the titular character.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:56.250
In addition to Li, the film has cast Mulan's
slapstick trio of fellow warriors Yao, Ling,

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:01.870
and Chien Po . Ling will be played by Jimmy
Wong, Po by Doua Moua, and Chen Tang will

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.600
be taking up the role of Yao, the so-called
"king of the rock."

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.060
One significant face missing from the action,
though?

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:08.880
Li Shang.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.150
The hunky commander has failed to show up
on any casting reports so far.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:17.210
Instead, it looks like the production team
has opted to split Shang's prominent character

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.630
into two separate personalities.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:23.940
Donnie Yen has been cast as the character
Commander Tung, who appears to be taking on

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.300
the role of Mulan's military commander.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.880
Separate from that relationship, we have Chen
Honghui, played by Yoson An.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.150
It appears that Chen Hongui will be a fellow
recruit in Tung's unit who bonds with Mulan

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.440
before the two form a romantic relationship.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.790
Of course, even the best cast isn't going
to get very far without a good group of people

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.780
working behind the scenes as well.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:50.010
Fortunately, the story of China's warrior-heroine
appears to be in good hands.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.730
Starting at the top, Disney has tapped Niki
Caro to helm the project.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.390
The Kiwi director has already drawn attention
thanks to her work on films like North Country,

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.380
The Zookeeper's Wife, and McFarland, USA.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.960
She first established herself in 2002 with
Whale Rider, a Maori film with feminist themes

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.380
of family, destiny, and generational divides
some obvious parallels with Mulan.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:17.100
For all of her past accomplishments, though,
a blockbuster like Mulan could launch Caro

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.380
to new heights.

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:23.000
In fact, the simple act of taking the job
made her the fourth woman to ever solo-direct

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.930
a film with a $100 million+ budget.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:29.900
If she manages to knock the project out of
the park, then the sky's the limit.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:35.060
Along with Caro, a team of four writers has
been brought on to adapt the story to a live-action

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:35.860
format.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.750
They include Rick Jaffa, Amanda Silver, Elizabeth
Martin, and Lauren Hynek.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:45.200
Jaffa and Silver are of particular interest,
as they have worked together on both Jurassic

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.020
World and the recent Planet of the Apes films.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:52.951
This gives them plenty of experience in bringing
classic stories into the modern era, which

00:04:52.951 --> 00:04:54.720
is encouraging, to say the least.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:05:00.170
Before we get too far into the possible direction
that the live-action remake could take, let's

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:05.430
take a quick trip down memory lane and revisit
just how Disney's 1998 animated version of

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.660
Mulan played out.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.380
The film takes place in ancient China, during
the Han Dynasty.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:15.500
In response to a Hun invasion, the Emperor
orders a full mobilization, including one

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.020
man from every family.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:21.880
This prompts Mulan to buck tradition and go
in her aged father's stead, disguised as a

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.720
young man.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:28.200
She is soon joined by the disgraced family
guardian, a tiny dragon named Mushu, and the

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.500
two manage to convince everyone that she can
bring the goods.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.920
After training with the other recruits, Mulan's
unit sets out to reinforce the imperial army,

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:40.990
only to find that they've already been annihilated
by the deadly Huns.

00:05:40.990 --> 00:05:46.300
Mulan heroically saves her brothers in arms
and, y'know, the whole of China by causing

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.640
an avalanche to sweep away the enemy during
an ambush.

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:54.720
In the process, though, she is revealed to
be a woman and is cast out of the army.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.780
Finding that some of the Huns, including their
leader Shan Yu, have survived the avalanche,

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:04.500
Mulan fearlessly follows the soldiers to the
imperial city, where she alerts everyone to

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.480
the approach of the Huns and helps foil their
attempt to kill the Emperor.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:13.600
Ultimately, Mulan is recognized for her heroic
deeds, and returns home to celebrations and

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:19.160
a visit from her commander Shang, whom she
invites to stay forever — uh, we mean, for

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:19.800
dinner.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:21.980
"Would you like to stay for dinner?"

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.280
"Would you like to stay forever?"

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.080
"Dinner would be great."

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:33.140
While the live-action remake will obviously
be leaning heavily on the '90s animated classic

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.850
for the bulk of its inspiration, there's also
the original Chinese legend itself which the

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:42.921
writers can draw from and based on the gritty
realism depicted in the trailer so far, it

00:06:42.921 --> 00:06:44.790
looks like they're doing just that.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:49.540
Of course, old stories like these almost always
have a ton of different versions over the

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.040
centuries.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.760
Naturally, this means the exact details of
the legend have varied over the years.

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:59.550
That said, Mulan's traditional story takes
place in ancient China during either the 4th

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.500
or 5th century.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.020
There are many distinctly similar factors
that modern audiences will recognize in the

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.110
tale as well.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:10.620
For instance, the story always starts with
a horde of barbarians invading China.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:15.320
This leads to Mulan volunteering to enlist
as her aged father's "son" in order to save

00:07:15.320 --> 00:07:18.840
him from having to go to war, where he'll
meet almost certain death.

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:24.840
She takes her family's heirloom weapons, joins
up with the army, and finds success as a soldier.

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.410
She even falls in love with an officer and
is offered a reward from the Emperor, at which

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:32.479
point she simply asks for a horse to ride
home.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:37.840
For all of the similarities across versions
of the story, there are also many things that

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.200
are completely different.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:44.080
For example, while the animated feature manages
to neatly fit everything into what feels like

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.760
a few weeks or possibly months, Mulan actually
fought in the ranks as a warrior for a decade.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.560
We're talking about a legitimate army career
here.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:56.660
Not only that, but she was eventually promoted
to general status.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:00.610
At one point, some stories explain that she
goes into battle dressed as a woman with the

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:05.220
specific intention of inspiring her men by
revealing her true identity.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:09.260
It works, and her soldiers gain an even greater
respect for her.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:13.740
While Mulan does eventually draw the attention
of the Emperor, it's not quite as epic as

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.150
the climactic finale of the '90s movie.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:21.520
Rather, the Emperor simply finds out that
his bravest soldier is a woman and, impressed,

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.620
offers her a reward.

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:27.460
She asks for a horse and rides home, only
to find that her father has died during her

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:31.060
long absence at least in some versions of
the story.

00:08:31.060 --> 00:08:35.510
This tragic ending gets even worse in some
accounts, as she is forced to become the wife

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.280
or concubine of an emperor.

00:08:37.469 --> 00:08:42.340
In the end, refusing to accept this fate,
China's greatest heroine ultimately takes

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:43.340
her own life.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:48.151
While he didn't have a ton of lines, Shan
Yu was a pretty important character in the

00:08:48.151 --> 00:08:53.560
original animated film, and it wasn't until
Mulan literally lit the man up over the imperial

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.780
city that everyone could breathe a collective
sigh of relief.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.880
Despite his importance, though, it appears
that the writers have actually decided to

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.780
ax the big bad from the remake.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:07.240
Instead, the production team is cashing in
on a little creative liberty and going in

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:10.690
a different if still quite intimidating direction.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:15.040
The film has brought in Gong Li, known for
her role in Memoirs of a Geisha, to play the

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:16.840
powerful witch Xian Lang.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:22.500
The official trailer also sets up another
villain, the warlord Bori Khan, but it appears

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.440
he will be little more than a frontman for
Lang's nefarious plans.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:31.300
This shift from brute force to the supernatural
is a curious one, and it'll be interesting

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.520
to see how it plays out on the big screen.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:38.440
A trailer also makes a deliberate attempt
to compare Mulan to a phoenix which traditionally

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:43.410
sits at the right hand of the emperor and
is his guardian and his protector while also

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:48.330
showing the witch literally turning into a
bird of prey, indicating a fowl showdown of

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.380
some sort or another is afoot.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:55.580
On top of that, one of the trailers even showcases
a duel between the two female warriors.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:10:00.700
Of course, what would a Mulan remake be without
the guardian of lost souls?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:05.670
The Eddie Murphy-voiced Mushu is one of the
most fondly-remembered elements of the original

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:06.800
animated classic.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:08.220
"You da man!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.260
...Well, sort of."

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.920
Mushu superfans should be careful before they
get their hopes too high when it comes to

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:15.900
the remake, though.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:20.100
While the fan blog DisInsider did report that
a source had claimed the little guy would

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:24.330
be in the film, very little information has
come out about what his actual role would

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:24.820
be.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.780
Will we see the powerful, the pleasurable,
the indestructible Mushu?

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:32.860
Or will we see a live-action alternative that
is more subdued and subtle?

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:37.320
Maybe we won't get an actual character at
all, but merely a quick glimpse of a small

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.800
dragon statue or some other Easter egg.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:44.110
So far, no one is reported to have been cast
in the role, which doesn't bode well for a

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.790
direct adaptation from the '90s original.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:51.190
However, fans can take comfort in the fact
that the cast list does contain an entry for

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:55.950
a character named Cricket, which hints that
perhaps Mushu's sidekick Cri-Kee will somehow

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:56.920
be represented.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.680
The official trailer seems to heavily imply
that the story will be steering into the "Mulan,

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.380
the phoenix" angle pretty hard.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:08.540
It even cuts to a shot of a live phoenix while
Mulan's father is asking the ancestors to

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:09.460
protect her.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:14.160
Perhaps instead of having no protector, we'll
simply be seeing Mushu swapped out for a more

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.680
appropriately epic phoenix guardian.

